# What each Russian letter arrives as: the code point a caller writes, and the
# byte of the module's alphabet the letter is read as.
#
# The module is US English's, and its Latin letters stay English's: a word in
# Latin letters inside Russian text is read by English's rules, as English.
# So Russian's letters take bytes no English word is written with, the ones
# the alphabet has for the accented letters of other Western languages --
# à to ÿ but ñ and ÷, with ß,  and  -- which it knows as
# letters already. ruru.statements says which of them is a vowel now, and
# generate_diaphones in rules/et_phone.dr asks for them before anything
# else, so none reaches the rule of the Latin letter it was an accent on.
# ь and ъ share a byte: neither says anything, and what each does to the
# letters beside it is the same.
#
# The cost is that an accented Latin letter inside Russian text is read as
# the Russian letter that took its byte. ñ, the n with a tilde, is left
#
# A capital arrives as its own small letter. Nothing in the module lowers a
# letter it was not written for, and nothing here wants to know a Russian
# letter was a capital.

0430 e0   # а
0431 e1   # б
0432 e2   # в
0433 e3   # г
0434 e4   # д
0435 e5   # е
0451 e6   # ё
0436 e7   # ж
0437 e8   # з
0438 e9   # и
0439 ea   # й
043a eb   # к
043b ec   # л
043c ed   # м
043d ee   # н
043e ef   # о
043f f0   # п
0440 f2   # р
0441 f3   # с
0442 f4   # т
0443 f5   # у
0444 f6   # ф
0445 f8   # х
0446 f9   # ц
0447 fa   # ч
0448 fb   # ш
0449 fc   # щ
044b fd   # ы
044c fe   # ь
044a fe   # ъ
044d f1   # э
044e df   # ю
044f 9c   # я

0410 e0   # А, as its small letter
0411 e1   # Б, as its small letter
0412 e2   # В, as its small letter
0413 e3   # Г, as its small letter
0414 e4   # Д, as its small letter
0415 e5   # Е, as its small letter
0401 e6   # Ё, as its small letter
0416 e7   # Ж, as its small letter
0417 e8   # З, as its small letter
0418 e9   # И, as its small letter
0419 ea   # Й, as its small letter
041a eb   # К, as its small letter
041b ec   # Л, as its small letter
041c ed   # М, as its small letter
041d ee   # Н, as its small letter
041e ef   # О, as its small letter
041f f0   # П, as its small letter
0420 f2   # Р, as its small letter
0421 f3   # С, as its small letter
0422 f4   # Т, as its small letter
0423 f5   # У, as its small letter
0424 f6   # Ф, as its small letter
0425 f8   # Х, as its small letter
0426 f9   # Ц, as its small letter
0427 fa   # Ч, as its small letter
0428 fb   # Ш, as its small letter
0429 fc   # Щ, as its small letter
042b fd   # Ы, as its small letter
042c fe   # Ь, as its small letter
042a fe   # Ъ, as its small letter
042d f1   # Э, as its small letter
042e df   # Ю, as its small letter
042f 9c   # Я, as its small letter

# The stress mark, the combining acute a writer puts after the vowel a word is
# stressed on: за́мок and замо́к. It is a letter that says nothing, and the
# stress rule reads it where it stands. It is how a dictionary says where a
# word is stressed, too.
0301 9a   # the stress mark

